cfFilterBannerToPDF: close the output stream on the success path

cfFilterBannerToPDF() never closes (or flushes) its output stream. When
it runs inside cfFilterChain(), as in the "universal" filter, the
parent closes the raw file descriptor and exits right after it returns,
so the buffered tail of the generated PDF (xref table and %%EOF) is
lost and the next filter, pdftopdf, gets a truncated PDF. The CUPS test
page (application/vnd.cups-pdf-banner) then fails with "universal
filter failed".

Backport of OpenPrinting/libcupsfilters#249 (fixes #212, merged
2026-09-14). Drop once the base's libcupsfilters includes it (see the
Containerfile's libcupsfilters-builder).

--- a/cupsfilters/bannertopdf.c
+++ b/cupsfilters/bannertopdf.c
@@ -1021,6 +1021,14 @@
   unlink(tempfile);
   if (inputfp)
     fclose(inputfp);
-  
+  // The output stream has to be flushed and closed here. When this filter
+  // function is called from cfFilterChain() (as the "universal" filter does),
+  // the parent closes the raw output file descriptor and exits right after
+  // this function returns, so a still buffered tail of the generated PDF
+  // (cross-reference table and "%%EOF") would be lost and the following
+  // filter in the chain would fail to parse the file.
+  if (outputfp)
+    fclose(outputfp);
+
   return (ret);
 }
